[244/1873] EvidenceGapMap
TITLE: Evidence Gap Map: Interactive Bubble-Chart Visualisation of Research Coverage Across Clinical Domains
TYPE: methods  |  ESTIMAND: Evidence coverage proportion by intervention-outcome cell
DATA: Systematic review databases with intervention-outcome classification matrices
PATH: C:\EvidenceGapMap

CURRENT BODY (155 words):
Can interactive gap-map visualisation identify under-researched intervention-outcome combinations more effectively than tabular summaries? We built a 7,652-line browser application implementing bubble-chart gap maps where each cell represents an intervention-outcome pair, with bubble size encoding study count and colour encoding certainty. The tool supports hierarchical intervention and outcome taxonomies, filtering by study design and risk of bias, and dynamic rescaling across clinical domains. Coverage analysis across the loaded evidence base showed that 34 percent of intervention-outcome cells contained no studies (95% CI 29 to 39), while 12 percent contained more than ten studies with moderate or high certainty evidence. Interactive filtering revealed that gaps concentrated in non-pharmacological interventions and patient-reported outcome domains where pharmaceutical-funded trials are less common. Visual gap mapping could prioritize research funding toward intervention-outcome combinations with the greatest evidence deficit relative to clinical importance. The tool depends on accurate pre-classified evidence matrices and cannot automatically assign interventions or outcomes from unstructured review text.

YOUR REWRITE (at most 156 words, 7 sentences):


